  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">CONSERVATION OF TIGER, RHINO, ELEPHANTS AND HOOLOCK GIBBONS IN KAZIRANGA-KARBI ANGLONG LANDSCAPE USING PNRM APPROACH BY FOREST DEPENDENT INDIGENOUS KARBI TRIBE IN KOHORA AND DIFFOLU RIVER BASINS, INDIA</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The purpose of this project is to (1) Strengthen and promote established sustainable conservation livelihood models with 100.forest-dependent families across six villages in the Kohora River Basin (KRB); (2) Design and test participatory, replicable eco.restoration models for recovery of habitats and connectivity corridors in the Kaziranga-Karbi Anglong Landscape; (3) Monitor.social, financial and ecological indicators annually to evaluate spatial and temporal project impacts on communities, key species and habitats in the KRB; (4) Create awareness among KRB communities and key stakeholders on ecosystem wellbeing, Participatory Natural Resource Management, sustainable livelihoods, and entrepreneurships; (5) Inventory and map non-timber forest products with sustainable management potential in the Diffolu River Basin (DRB); (6) Develop natural resource-based.sustainable livelihood and entrepreneurship models involving 100 households to improve habitat and quality of life in the DRB;.and (7) Participatory drafting of the prospective Villages Natural Resource Management Plan.</narrative>
  </description>
